   "claims": [
    "Sphere The surface area (SA) of a sphere can be calculated using the equation: SA = 4πr2 where r is the radius Xael doesn't like sharing her chocolate truffles with anyone.",
    "Given that each truffle has a radius of 0.325 inches: SA = 4 × π × 0.3252 = 1.327 in2 Cone The surface area of a circular cone can be calculated by summing the surface area of each of its individual components.",
    "She custom orders a Rubik's Cube in which all the faces are black, and has to pay for the customization based on the surface area of the cube with an edge length of 4 inches.",
    "He is curious whether his heated water cools faster than when in a bathtub, and needs to calculate the surface area of his cylindrical tank of height 5.5 feet and radius of 3.5 feet.",
    "Given each capsule has r of 0.05 inches and h of 0.5 inches: SA = 4π × 0.052 + 2π × 0.05 × 0.5 = 0.188 in2 Spherical Cap The surface area of a spherical cap is based on the height of the segment in question."
   ],
